## A new beginning after cancer treatment

Finishing oncological treatment is a milestone — but it is far from the end of the journey. Chemotherapy, radiotherapy and other forms of treatment leave traces on both body and mind that do not heal overnight. Fatigue, pain, a weakened immune system, lymphoedema or psychological exhaustion accompany many patients for months after their therapy ends.

It is precisely for these people that the medical team at Ensana in Mariánské Lázně has developed a specialised post-oncology programme — comprehensive spa care that combines natural healing resources, modern medicine and an individual approach.

## Where the programme takes place

The programme was created by Ensana's team of physicians and therapists in Mariánské Lázně, and that is where guests can take part. You can choose between two hotels:

### Ensana Nové Lázně

A five-star hotel with a rich history, direct access to natural healing springs and a historic Roman bath. It delivers the highest standard of care and satisfies even the most discerning guests. [More about Ensana Nové Lázně](/en/hotel/nove-lazne).

### Ensana Hvězda

One of the finest spa hotels in town. It combines four-star accommodation and modern wellness with a welcoming atmosphere — professional care and comfort under one roof. [More about Ensana Hvězda](/en/hotel/hvezda).

Both hotels are situated in the heart of the spa town yet surrounded by nature. Quiet and fresh air are key factors for effective recovery of body and mind.

## Who the programme is designed for

The post-oncology programme is designed for guests who have completed cancer treatment and need to restore their physical and mental strength. Whether the treatment involved chemotherapy, radiotherapy or another form of therapy, the programme is tailored to address specific needs during remission and support the return to everyday life.

It is especially beneficial for people dealing with:

- **lymphoedema** following surgery or radiation,
- **loss of vitality** and persistent fatigue,
- **pain** in the musculoskeletal or nervous system,
- **weakened immunity** after demanding treatment,
- **psychological exhaustion** and the need for gentle recovery under expert supervision.

The programme also encourages lasting change. Through practical advice, it motivates guests to maintain a healthier lifestyle, which may reduce the risk of recurrence.

## What to expect from the programme

The minimum stay is seven nights. Throughout your visit, you will receive nutritious breakfasts, lunches and dinners prepared with a focus on supporting recovery and the immune system.

The programme begins with an **initial medical examination**, during which a specialist assesses your current health and needs and defines your convalescence goals. Based on this assessment, an individual treatment plan is created, typically including:

- **therapies using natural healing resources** — [mineral baths](/en/mineral-springs) and carbonated baths that promote regeneration and strengthen the body's defences,
- **regular check-ups and medical consultations** allowing ongoing adjustment of care to match your current condition,
- **nutritional counselling** focused on restoring vitality, boosting immunity and building healthy eating habits after a demanding treatment period,
- **psychological support and relaxation** through targeted techniques — massage, breathing exercises or mindfulness practices that help manage stress and improve sleep quality,
- **a stay in a safe, tranquil environment** that creates space for genuine healing.

## What treatments the programme includes

As part of the daily programme, you will undergo up to three treatments per day prescribed by the spa physician:

### Classic healing treatments

- mineral baths,
- dry CO₂ gas baths,
- [drinking cures](/en/magazine/spa-treatment-guide) from local healing springs.

### Targeted therapies for restoring fitness

- aquatic exercise,
- individual physiotherapy.

### Supportive care

- paraffin hand wraps,
- oxygen therapy.

### Nutritional and laboratory support

- body composition analysis,
- personalised dietary plan and practical advice for the recovery period,
- blood tests monitoring glucose, cholesterol, liver and kidney function and other important markers.

And most importantly — if you have any questions, you can turn to the medical and nursing team at any time during your stay.

## Why Mariánské Lázně

Mariánské Lázně brings together everything that matters for post-oncology recovery: natural healing resources with a [tradition spanning over two centuries](/en/history), an outstanding medical team, a peaceful setting amid nature, and certified climatic conditions that in themselves support healing and renewal.

Ensana's post-oncology programme is not simply a spa stay. It is a structured, medically guided path back to a full life.
